# INITIAL PUBLICATION POLICY: deny by default, permit reviewed source types.
# This does not inspect content or remove already tracked files.
# Root Python modules retain their original names and locations.
*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/requirements.txt
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/*.py

# Explicit documentation candidates. Review the LOCAL copies before staging.
!/GC_audit_1_3_12_felbontasi_profilok.md
!/GC_1_0_19_NDOG_NWOG_celarak.md
!/QQQ_options_advisor_utmutato.md
!/ES_NQ_regime_v12_utmutato.md
!/ICT_market_transition_es_GC_breaker_utmutato.md
!/VIX_stress_monitor_utmutato.md
!/Makro_AI_bankhitel_console_utmutato.md

# Defense in depth: never allow likely local/private Python files by wildcard.
# If a necessary module matches one of these names, review it first.
local_*.py
*_local.py
*secret*.py
*credential*.py
*_backup.py
*_old.py

# No subdirectory is enabled yet. This intentionally excludes venv, .idea,
# raw data, outputs, caches, source archives, screenshots and nested fixtures.
# JSON/CSV are NOT globally forbidden in python_pub. Within this toolkit,
# add exact exceptions only after content, necessity and redistribution review.
# In particular, macro_provider_snapshot.json and tests/fixtures/ are withheld.
# Never bypass this policy with git add -f.
